    "source_review": {
      "revert_helpers": "Both helpers call the common process-fatal reversion helper. On Windows it attempts TerminateProcess; regardless of return or wrapper failure, os._exit(70) follows. In the fault-injected test path the helper raises GuardianServiceThreadFatalError, a BaseException subclass.",
      "request_handler": "The OS-token route catches GuardianServiceThreadFatalError before the broad BaseException handler and fail-stops before cleanup/receipt/response; integration negative asserts those side effects do not happen.",
      "token_close_order": "Both paths attempt token-handle close and RevertToSelf; reversion failure process-fatal takes precedence. A source token close failure is surfaced only after successful reversion.",
      "parent_gate": "Frozen parent source manifest checks require the fixed worker/helper/bootstrap sources; negative test removes worker/bootstrap/helper entries and requires rejection.",
      "format_drift": "ruff format --check reports only parent_launcher.py and test_ctp_i13_source_manifest_candidate.py; service and service tests are already formatted. Record as whole-file pre-existing drift, not a new logic failure."
    },
    "scope": "Pre-orchestration helper and parent-manifest QA only. Snapshot explicitly predates protected per-request supervisor/Job orchestration. No SCM install/ACL mutation/provider/native/private config. Production TerminateProcess/os._exit were not invoked by tests.",
